;; firebar-sprites.ab3 -- can the firebars' balls be hardware sprites instead of bobs?
;; Compile in UAE (S/run-proof). Not part of the game. 2-4 on NTSC runs over budget where three short firebars (18 balls, each a
;; BBlit: its background saved, cut in, restored) meet the lifts and the fire frenzy (the main project's OPTIMISATION note, entry 16). A
;; hardware sprite costs no blit at all: the chip set draws it over the playfields from a few words in Chip RAM.
;;
;; The idea. A ball is 8x8 in three pens (11 red, 4 orange, 8 white): one 16 px sprite channel, 3 colours, no attaching, so all
;; eight channels are free for balls. Eight is not enough for 18, so each channel is multiplexed down the screen: when a sprite
;; ends, the hardware reads the next two words of its data as new control words, so a channel's data can be ball, control
;; words, ball, ... and two zero words to end. A ball may follow another in the same channel only from one line below the
;; other's end (the line the control words are read). Each frame the visible balls are sorted by y and dealt to the first
;; channel that is free at their line; any ball no channel can take (a level bar puts six on the same lines) is drawn as a bob.
;;
;; How the sprites are driven. Not with DisplaySprite: the copper list's sprite block (the CopList object's long at offset 12,
;; displaylib.ab3's NEWTYPE .mycop) holds, for each channel, MOVEs to SPRxPOS, SPRxCTL, SPRxPTH and SPRxPTL; InitCopList writes the
;; registers and this proof pokes the data words: the first ball's position and the channel's data in Chip RAM. The data is
;; double buffered (written for the next frame while the hardware reads this frame's) and the block is poked after VWait, before
;; the world list's first line. The colours: sprite bank 2 (entries 32 to 47; DisplayControls ..., $33 as sprite-over-hud.ab3,
;; whose sprite x matched the bitmap with no bias), the same three colours for each channel pair.
;;
;; The display is the game's (the first run, PAL's lines on an NTSC machine, ran the world list past the frame): a 16 line HUD list over a 208 line world list, 3 lines apart, the world dual playfield at fetch mode
;; 3, DisplayAdjust -1 and -1, the lores sprite flag ($400) on both type words. The world list has 7 sprites. The fireball's
;; pictures are the game's (game/assets/items-16x16.iff, cell 28), cut as the game cuts them.
;;
;; It runs by itself (sixth run on: Esc quits early). Six runs, one after the other, from the same start each time (the camera at
;; the left, every bar at angle 0): fetch mode 3 (the game's), 1 and 0, each as bobs and then as sprites, each 4 sweeps of the
;; camera there and back at 2 px a frame (about 3.5 minutes on PAL in all). A sprite run deals the balls to the channels its fetch
;; mode leaves (the fifth run: 1 at fetch mode 3, 5 at 1, all 7 at 0; the world list has 7) and draws the rest as bobs. Found on
;; the way: a channel's chain of balls works (the third run); fetch mode 3's early fetch for the scroll takes the DMA slots of
;; every channel but 0 (the fourth and fifth runs, with 8 and with 7 channels).
;;
;; What to look at and report: nothing to press; watch for anything wrong in any run (a missing or misplaced ball in the second,
;; fourth or sixth run, the sprite ones; stray lines or specks; flicker), then the results file: each run's draw time (lines
;; from the start of the work until the blitter is idle), how many frames ran late, and how many balls fell back to bobs.

;; The 68020 optimizer, as the game (the main project's OPTIMISATION note, entry 8): without it a division is a library call of about 2
;; lines, and the first run's sprite build (four or so a ball) cost 165 lines a frame.
OPTIMIZE 1

WBStartup

;; =======================================================
;; CONSTANTS
;; =======================================================

#RAW_KEY_SPACE = $40
#RAW_KEY_ESC   = $45
#RAW_KEY_M     = $37
#RAW_KEY_T     = $14
#RAW_KEY_F     = $23
#RAW_KEY_S     = $21

#HUD_YPOS_PAL  = 44
#HUD_YPOS_NTSC = 32
#HUD_H      = 16
#LIST_GAP   = 3
#VIEW_H     = 208
#VIEW_TOP   = 32
#VIEW_W     = 320
#COPPER_COLORS = 48

;; The game's type words ($13014 and $13038) with the lores sprite flag.
#HUD_FLAGS   = $13414
#WORLD_FLAGS = $13438
;; The same at fetch mode 0; F adds $1000 a step (the game's is 3).
#WORLD_FLAGS_FMODE0 = $10438

#DISPLAY_ADJUST_START = -1
#DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP  = -1
#PLAYFIELD2_OFFSET_16 = $1c00
#BANK_XOR      = $33

;; Bitmaps: 0 and 1 the front pair, 2 the back, 3 the HUD band, 4 the items sheet.
#BM_A     = 0
#BM_B     = 1
#BM_BACK  = 2
#BM_HUD   = 3
#BM_ITEMS = 4
#FRONT_W  = 1024
#BACK_W   = 1152
#WORLD_H  = 256
#HUD_W    = 384
#ITEMS_W  = 992
#ITEMS_H  = 16

#TILE                = 16
#BALL                = 8
#BALL_CELL           = 28
#PRE_BALL            = 0
#BOB_BYTES           = 16384
#BARS                = 3
#PARTS               = 6
#ANGLES              = 32
#MAX_BALLS           = 48
#CHANNELS            = 8
#CHANNEL_BALLS       = 16
#CHANNEL_BYTES       = 640
#MYCOP_SPRITES       = 12
#MYCOP_YPOS          = 48
#SPRITE_H_OFFSET     = 128
#WORK_LINE           = 70
#CAMERA_MIN          = 160
#CAMERA_MAX          = 560
#CAMERA_STEP         = 2
#RUNS                = 6
#RUN_TRIPS           = 4
#RUN_SETTLE          = 10

;; =======================================================
;; GLOBALS
;; =======================================================

Dim ballWord.l(4*#BALL - 1)
Dim partOffsetX.w(#ANGLES*#PARTS - 1)
Dim partOffsetY.w(#ANGLES*#PARTS - 1)
Dim barCentreX.w(#BARS - 1)
Dim barCentreY.w(#BARS - 1)
Dim barAngle.w(#BARS - 1)
Dim barSpeed.w(#BARS - 1)
Dim ballScreenX.w(#MAX_BALLS - 1)
Dim ballScreenY.w(#MAX_BALLS - 1)
Dim ballOrder.w(#MAX_BALLS - 1)
Dim channelBuffer.l(2*#CHANNELS - 1)
Dim channelNextY.w(#CHANNELS - 1)
Dim channelFill.w(#CHANNELS - 1)
Dim channelCount.w(#CHANNELS - 1)
Dim channelPos.l(#CHANNELS - 1)
Dim channelCtl.l(#CHANNELS - 1)

quitFlag.w = False
;; The lists' first line, as the game's: the top of the standard PAL window, or line 32 on an NTSC machine.
hudYpos.w = #HUD_YPOS_PAL
If NTSC = True Then hudYpos = #HUD_YPOS_NTSC
drawBm.w = #BM_B
drawBuf.w = 1
frameCount.l = 0
spriteMode.w = True
cameraMoving.w = True
mWasDown.w = False
testColumn.w = False
fWasDown.w = False
worldFetch.w = 3
listSprites.w = 7
;; The runs: fetch mode 3 (the game's), 1 and 0, each as bobs then as sprites, and how far each has got.
Dim runFetch.w(#RUNS - 1)
Dim runSprites.w(#RUNS - 1)
runFetch(0) = 3
runFetch(1) = 3
runFetch(2) = 1
runFetch(3) = 1
runFetch(4) = 0
runFetch(5) = 0
For runNumber.w = 0 To #RUNS - 1
  runSprites(runNumber) = False
  If (runNumber AND 1) = 1 Then runSprites(runNumber) = True
Next
Dim runFrames.l(#RUNS - 1)
Dim runSum.l(#RUNS - 1)
Dim runWorst.l(#RUNS - 1)
Dim runLate.l(#RUNS - 1)
Dim runFellBack.l(#RUNS - 1)
runIndex.w = 0
runFrame.l = 0
tripsDone.w = 0
usableChannels.w = 7
;; The lines in a frame, by the machine's standard.
frameLines.w = 312
If NTSC = True Then frameLines = 262
sWasDown.w = False
Dim fetchSeen.w(3)
tWasDown.w = False
Dim dumpWord.l(39)
dumpFrame.l = 0
spaceWasDown.w = False
cameraX.w = #CAMERA_MIN
cameraStep.w = 1
ballCount.w = 0
bufferSet.w = 0
spriteBlock.l = 0
listTop.w = 0
nullBlock.l = 0
spinFrame.w = 0
startLine.l = 0
endLine.l = 0
workLines.l = 0
Dim modeFrames.l(7)
Dim modeSum.l(7)
Dim modeWorst.l(7)
overflowFrames.l = 0
overflowWorst.w = 0
overflowSum.l = 0
channelsWorst.w = 0
ballsWorst.w = 0
chipBefore.l = 0
chipAfter.l = 0
itemsLoaded.w = False

;; =======================================================
;; ALLOC AND FILES (AMIGA MODE)
;; =======================================================

BitMap #BM_A, #FRONT_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_B, #FRONT_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_BACK, #BACK_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_HUD, #HUD_W, #HUD_H, 4
BitMap #BM_ITEMS, #ITEMS_W, #ITEMS_H, 4
If Exists("sparky-dave:game/assets/items-16x16.iff") > 0
  LoadBitMap #BM_ITEMS, "sparky-dave:game/assets/items-16x16.iff"
  itemsLoaded = True
EndIf

;; The channels' data, two sets (this frame's and the next's), and 16 zero bytes for a channel with nothing to show.
chipBefore = AvailMem_(2)
For bufferIndex.w = 0 To 2*#CHANNELS - 1
  channelBuffer(bufferIndex) = AllocMem_(#CHANNEL_BYTES, $10002)
Next
nullBlock = AllocMem_(16, $10002)
chipAfter = AvailMem_(2)

;; 0 black (the castle); 1 grey (the blocks and floor); 4 orange, 8 white, 11 red (the fireball's pens, the game's colours);
;; 7 white (the HUD's marks); 16 to 31 the back, all black; 33 to 35, 37 to 39, 41 to 43, 45 to 47 each channel pair's colours
;; 1 to 3: red, orange, white (pens 11, 4 and 8).
InitPalette 0, #COPPER_COLORS
AGAPalRGB 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
AGAPalRGB 0, 1, 170, 170, 170
AGAPalRGB 0, 4, 230, 156, 33
AGAPalRGB 0, 7, 255, 255, 255
AGAPalRGB 0, 8, 255, 255, 255
AGAPalRGB 0, 11, 181, 50, 32
For pairIndex.w = 0 To 3
  AGAPalRGB 0, 33 + pairIndex*4, 181, 50, 32
  AGAPalRGB 0, 34 + pairIndex*4, 230, 156, 33
  AGAPalRGB 0, 35 + pairIndex*4, 255, 255, 255
Next

;; The bars: their centres (each on a grey block), their speeds in 256ths of a turn a frame (two one way, one the other), and
;; every part's offset at every one of 32 angles (part 0 the centre, then 8 px apart), clockwise from straight up.
barCentreX(0) = 408
barCentreY(0) = 120
barCentreX(1) = 520
barCentreY(1) = 104
barCentreX(2) = 632
barCentreY(2) = 136
barSpeed(0) = 3
barSpeed(1) = -4
barSpeed(2) = 2
;; A float step: the literal in a word expression overflowed the compiler (it types the sum by its first term).
angleStep.f = 6.2831853
angleStep = angleStep/#ANGLES
For angleIndex.w = 0 To #ANGLES - 1
  angleRadians.f = angleStep
  angleRadians = angleRadians*angleIndex
  For partIndex.w = 0 To #PARTS - 1
    partOffsetX(angleIndex*#PARTS + partIndex) = Int(Sin(angleRadians)*partIndex*8 + 0.5)
    partOffsetY(angleIndex*#PARTS + partIndex) = -Int(Cos(angleRadians)*partIndex*8 + 0.5)
  Next
Next

;; =======================================================
;; DISPLAY (BLITZ MODE)
;; =======================================================

BLITZ

Buffer 0, #BOB_BYTES
Buffer 1, #BOB_BYTES

;; Beam line: VPOSR bit 0 is V8, VHPOSR high byte V0 to V7. Masked before dividing because bit 31 is a flag and the long is negative.
Function.l RasterLine{}
  rawPosition.l = Peek.l($dff004)
  Function Return (rawPosition AND $1ff00)/256
End Function

;; The castle: black, a grey floor, a grey block under each bar's centre, grey pillars.
Statement DrawFront{bitmapIndex.w}
  SHARED barCentreX(), barCentreY()
  Use BitMap bitmapIndex
  Cls 0
  Boxf 0, 208, #FRONT_W - 1, 239, 1
  For pillarX.w = 64 To #FRONT_W - 64 Step 192
    Boxf pillarX, 160, pillarX + 15, 207, 1
  Next
  For barIndex.w = 0 To #BARS - 1
    Boxf barCentreX(barIndex) - 8, barCentreY(barIndex) - 8, barCentreX(barIndex) + 7, barCentreY(barIndex) + 7, 1
  Next
End Statement

;; The fireball's four pictures (the game's cut: cell 28's four 8x8 quarters, small to large) as shapes for the bobs, and as
;; sprite rows: each row a long, plane 0's word then plane 1's, the 8 px in the word's top byte; pen 11 is colour 1, pen 4
;; colour 2, pen 8 colour 3. Without the sheet, a plain ball in the same three colours.
Statement MakeBall{}
  SHARED ballWord(), itemsLoaded
  Use BitMap #BM_ITEMS
  If itemsLoaded = False
    Cls 0
    For frameIndex.w = 0 To 3
      cellLeft.w = #BALL_CELL*#TILE + (frameIndex AND 1)*#BALL
      cellTop.w = (frameIndex/2)*#BALL
      Boxf cellLeft + 1, cellTop + 1, cellLeft + 6, cellTop + 6, 11
      Boxf cellLeft + 2, cellTop + 2, cellLeft + 5, cellTop + 5, 4
      Boxf cellLeft + 3, cellTop + 3, cellLeft + 3 + (frameIndex AND 1), cellTop + 4, 8
    Next
  EndIf
  For frameIndex.w = 0 To 3
    cellLeft.w = #BALL_CELL*#TILE + (frameIndex AND 1)*#BALL
    cellTop.w = (frameIndex/2)*#BALL
    GetaShape #PRE_BALL + frameIndex, cellLeft, cellTop, #BALL, #BALL
    For rowIndex.w = 0 To #BALL - 1
      planeZero.l = 0
      planeOne.l = 0
      For columnIndex.w = 0 To #BALL - 1
        pixelPen.w = Point(cellLeft + columnIndex, cellTop + rowIndex)
        bitValue.l = 1
        For shiftIndex.w = 1 To 15 - columnIndex
          bitValue = bitValue*2
        Next
        If pixelPen = 11 OR pixelPen = 8 Then planeZero = planeZero + bitValue
        If pixelPen = 4 OR pixelPen = 8 Then planeOne = planeOne + bitValue
      Next
      ballWord(frameIndex*#BALL + rowIndex) = planeZero*65536 + planeOne
    Next
  Next
End Statement

;; The balls the screen shows this frame, in screen coordinates (x from the view's left, y from the world list's first line).
Statement GatherBalls{}
  SHARED barCentreX(), barCentreY(), barAngle(), partOffsetX(), partOffsetY(), ballScreenX(), ballScreenY(), ballCount, cameraX
  ballCount = 0
  For barIndex.w = 0 To #BARS - 1
    offsetBase.w = ((barAngle(barIndex)/8) AND (#ANGLES - 1))*#PARTS
    For partIndex.w = 0 To #PARTS - 1
      screenX.w = barCentreX(barIndex) - #BALL/2 + partOffsetX(offsetBase + partIndex) - cameraX
      screenY.w = barCentreY(barIndex) - #BALL/2 + partOffsetY(offsetBase + partIndex) - #VIEW_TOP
      If screenX > -#BALL AND screenX < #VIEW_W AND screenY >= 1 AND screenY + #BALL <= #VIEW_H - 1
        If ballCount < #MAX_BALLS
          ballScreenX(ballCount) = screenX
          ballScreenY(ballCount) = screenY
          ballCount = ballCount + 1
        EndIf
      EndIf
    Next
  Next
End Statement

;; The game's way: every ball a bob.
Statement DrawBallBobs{}
  SHARED ballScreenX(), ballScreenY(), ballCount, cameraX, spinFrame, drawBuf
  For ballIndex.w = 0 To ballCount - 1
    BBlit drawBuf, #PRE_BALL + spinFrame, ballScreenX(ballIndex) + cameraX, ballScreenY(ballIndex) + #VIEW_TOP
  Next
End Statement

;; Sprites: the balls by y, each to the first channel free at its line, its control words and rows into that channel's data
;; for the next frame; a ball none can take is a bob. Returns how many fell back.
Function.w BuildSprites{}
  SHARED ballScreenX(), ballScreenY(), ballOrder(), ballCount, cameraX, spinFrame, drawBuf, ballWord(), listTop, bufferSet
  SHARED channelBuffer(), channelNextY(), channelFill(), channelCount(), channelPos(), channelCtl(), usableChannels
  For ballIndex.w = 0 To ballCount - 1
    ballOrder(ballIndex) = ballIndex
  Next
  For ballIndex = 1 To ballCount - 1
    movingBall.w = ballOrder(ballIndex)
    placeIndex.w = ballIndex
    keepMoving.w = True
    While placeIndex > 0 AND keepMoving = True
      If ballScreenY(ballOrder(placeIndex - 1)) > ballScreenY(movingBall)
        ballOrder(placeIndex) = ballOrder(placeIndex - 1)
        placeIndex = placeIndex - 1
      Else
        keepMoving = False
      EndIf
    Wend
    ballOrder(placeIndex) = movingBall
  Next
  For channelIndex.w = 0 To #CHANNELS - 1
    channelNextY(channelIndex) = -100
    channelFill(channelIndex) = 0
    channelCount(channelIndex) = 0
  Next
  fellBack.w = 0
  For orderIndex.w = 0 To ballCount - 1
    ballIndex = ballOrder(orderIndex)
    screenY.w = ballScreenY(ballIndex)
    takenBy.w = -1
    channelIndex = 0
    While takenBy = -1 AND channelIndex < usableChannels
      If screenY >= channelNextY(channelIndex) AND channelCount(channelIndex) < #CHANNEL_BALLS Then takenBy = channelIndex
      channelIndex = channelIndex + 1
    Wend
    If takenBy = -1
      BBlit drawBuf, #PRE_BALL + spinFrame, ballScreenX(ballIndex) + cameraX, screenY + #VIEW_TOP
      fellBack = fellBack + 1
    Else
      vStart.w = listTop + screenY
      vStop.w = vStart + #BALL
      hStart.w = ballScreenX(ballIndex) + #SPRITE_H_OFFSET
      posWord.l = (vStart AND 255)*256 + ((hStart/2) AND 255)
      ctlWord.l = (vStop AND 255)*256 + (vStart AND 256)/64 + (vStop AND 256)/128 + (hStart AND 1)
      dataAddress.l = channelBuffer(bufferSet*#CHANNELS + takenBy) + channelFill(takenBy)
      If channelCount(takenBy) = 0
        channelPos(takenBy) = posWord
        channelCtl(takenBy) = ctlWord
      Else
        Poke.w dataAddress, posWord
        Poke.w dataAddress + 2, ctlWord
        dataAddress = dataAddress + 4
        channelFill(takenBy) = channelFill(takenBy) + 4
      EndIf
      wordBase.w = spinFrame*#BALL
      For rowIndex.w = 0 To #BALL - 1
        Poke.l dataAddress + rowIndex*4, ballWord(wordBase + rowIndex)
      Next
      channelFill(takenBy) = channelFill(takenBy) + #BALL*4
      channelCount(takenBy) = channelCount(takenBy) + 1
      channelNextY(takenBy) = screenY + #BALL + 1
    EndIf
  Next
  For channelIndex = 0 To #CHANNELS - 1
    If channelCount(channelIndex) > 0
      Poke.l channelBuffer(bufferSet*#CHANNELS + channelIndex) + channelFill(channelIndex), 0
    EndIf
  Next
  Function Return fellBack
End Function

;; After VWait, before the world list's first line: each channel's first ball's position and its data (this frame's set), or off.
Statement PokeSpriteBlock{}
  SHARED spriteBlock, channelBuffer(), channelCount(), channelPos(), channelCtl(), bufferSet, nullBlock, spriteMode, listSprites
  For channelIndex.w = 0 To listSprites - 1
    entryAddress.l = spriteBlock + channelIndex*16
    dataAddress.l = nullBlock
    If spriteMode = True AND channelCount(channelIndex) > 0
      Poke.w entryAddress + 2, channelPos(channelIndex)
      Poke.w entryAddress + 6, channelCtl(channelIndex)
      dataAddress = channelBuffer(bufferSet*#CHANNELS + channelIndex)
    Else
      Poke.w entryAddress + 2, 0
      Poke.w entryAddress + 6, 0
    EndIf
    Poke.w entryAddress + 10, (dataAddress/65536) AND $FFFF
    Poke.w entryAddress + 14, dataAddress AND $FFFF
  Next
End Statement

;; The two lists, made again when F changes the world list's fetch mode (#WORLD_FLAGS_FMODE0 plus worldFetch*$1000): sprite bank
;; 2 (entries 32 to 47) on both, the back's colours at 16 to 31 as in the game, every channel off before the display starts.
Statement SetupDisplay{}
  SHARED hudYpos, worldFetch, spriteBlock, listTop, channelCount(), drawBm, cameraX, listSprites
  InitCopList 0, hudYpos, #HUD_H, #HUD_FLAGS, 0, #COPPER_COLORS, 0
  InitCopList 1, hudYpos + #HUD_H + #LIST_GAP, #VIEW_H, #WORLD_FLAGS_FMODE0 + worldFetch*$1000, listSprites, 0, 0
  DisplayControls 0, 0, 0, #BANK_XOR
  DisplayControls 1, 0, #PLAYFIELD2_OFFSET_16, #BANK_XOR
  DisplayAdjust 0, 0, 0, 0, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_START, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP
  DisplayAdjust 1, 0, 0, 0, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_START, #DISPLAY_ADJUST_STOP
  spriteBlock = Peek.l(Addr CopList(1) + #MYCOP_SPRITES)
  listTop = Peek.w(Addr CopList(1) + #MYCOP_YPOS)
  For channelIndex.w = 0 To #CHANNELS - 1
    channelCount(channelIndex) = 0
  Next
  If spriteBlock <> 0 Then PokeSpriteBlock{}
  CreateDisplay 0, 1
  DisplayPalette 0, 0
  DisplayBitMap 0, #BM_HUD, 0, 0
  DisplayBitMap 1, drawBm, cameraX, #VIEW_TOP, #BM_BACK, 0, #VIEW_TOP
End Statement

BBlitMode CookieMode
SpriteMode 0
MakeBall{}
DrawFront{#BM_A}
DrawFront{#BM_B}
Use BitMap #BM_BACK
Cls 0
Use BitMap #BM_HUD
Cls 0
For tickX.w = 20 To #HUD_W - 20 Step 20
  Boxf tickX, 0, tickX, 1, 7
  Boxf tickX, 14, tickX, 15, 7
Next

SetupDisplay{}
BlitzKeys On

;; The runs, one after the other with nothing to press: each a fetch mode and bobs or sprites, from the same start (the camera at
;; #CAMERA_MIN, every bar at angle 0, the spin's count at 0), for #RUN_TRIPS sweeps of the camera there and back, 2 px a frame.
While quitFlag = False
  If RawStatus(#RAW_KEY_ESC) Then quitFlag = True

  If runFrame = 0
    If runFetch(runIndex) <> worldFetch
      worldFetch = runFetch(runIndex)
      VWait
      SetupDisplay{}
    EndIf
    spriteMode = runSprites(runIndex)
    usableChannels = 7
    If worldFetch = 1 OR worldFetch = 2 Then usableChannels = 5
    If worldFetch = 3 Then usableChannels = 1
    cameraX = #CAMERA_MIN
    cameraStep = #CAMERA_STEP
    tripsDone = 0
    For barIndex.w = 0 To #BARS - 1
      barAngle(barIndex) = 0
    Next
  EndIf

  cameraX = cameraX + cameraStep
  If cameraX >= #CAMERA_MAX Then cameraStep = -#CAMERA_STEP
  If cameraX <= #CAMERA_MIN
    cameraStep = #CAMERA_STEP
    tripsDone = tripsDone + 1
  EndIf
  For barIndex.w = 0 To #BARS - 1
    barAngle(barIndex) = (barAngle(barIndex) + barSpeed(barIndex)) AND 255
  Next
  spinFrame = (runFrame/4) AND 3
  bufferSet = frameCount AND 1

  ;; The work, timed from a fixed line until the blitter is idle: the bobs' restore, then the balls one way or the other.
  While RasterLine{} < #WORK_LINE
  Wend
  Use BitMap drawBm
  startLine = RasterLine{}
  UnBuffer drawBuf
  GatherBalls{}
  fellBack.w = 0
  If spriteMode = True
    fellBack = BuildSprites{}
  Else
    DrawBallBobs{}
    For channelIndex = 0 To #CHANNELS - 1
      channelCount(channelIndex) = 0
    Next
  EndIf
  While (Peek.w($dff002) AND $4000) <> 0
  Wend
  endLine = RasterLine{}
  workLines = endLine - startLine
  If workLines < 0 Then workLines = workLines + frameLines
  If runFrame >= #RUN_SETTLE
    runFrames(runIndex) = runFrames(runIndex) + 1
    runSum(runIndex) = runSum(runIndex) + workLines
    If workLines > runWorst(runIndex) Then runWorst(runIndex) = workLines
    If #WORK_LINE + workLines >= frameLines Then runLate(runIndex) = runLate(runIndex) + 1
    runFellBack(runIndex) = runFellBack(runIndex) + fellBack
    If ballCount > ballsWorst Then ballsWorst = ballCount
  EndIf

  VWait
  DisplayBitMap 1, drawBm, cameraX, #VIEW_TOP, #BM_BACK, 0, #VIEW_TOP
  If spriteBlock <> 0 Then PokeSpriteBlock{}
  If drawBm = #BM_A
    drawBm = #BM_B
    drawBuf = 1
  Else
    drawBm = #BM_A
    drawBuf = 0
  EndIf
  frameCount = frameCount + 1
  runFrame = runFrame + 1
  If tripsDone >= #RUN_TRIPS
    runIndex = runIndex + 1
    runFrame = 0
    If runIndex >= #RUNS Then quitFlag = True
  EndIf
Wend

AMIGA
For bufferIndex = 0 To 2*#CHANNELS - 1
  FreeMem_ channelBuffer(bufferIndex), #CHANNEL_BYTES
Next
FreeMem_ nullBlock, 16
If WriteFile(0, "sparky-dave:game/proofs/results/firebar-sprites-results.txt")
  FileOutput 0
  NPrint "firebar-sprites: HUD $", Hex$(#HUD_FLAGS), ", world $", Hex$(#WORLD_FLAGS), ", ", frameCount, " frames"
  NPrint "items sheet loaded (the game's fireball): ", itemsLoaded, "; sprite block found: ", spriteBlock <> 0, "; world list top line: ", listTop
  NPrint "lines a frame (the latest beam line seen): ", frameLines + 1
  NPrint "runs finished: ", runIndex, " of ", #RUNS, " (each ", #RUN_TRIPS, " sweeps of the camera there and back; the first ", #RUN_SETTLE, " frames of a run left out)"
  NPrint "the work (from line ", #WORK_LINE, ": the bobs' restore and the balls, until the blitter is idle), in lines; late is a frame"
  NPrint "whose work reached the end of the frame; fell back is balls drawn as bobs in a sprite run (no channel free at their line):"
  For runNumber.w = 0 To #RUNS - 1
    If runFrames(runNumber) > 0
      kindName$ = "bobs   "
      If runSprites(runNumber) = True Then kindName$ = "sprites"
      averageLines.l = runSum(runNumber)/runFrames(runNumber)
      NPrint "  fetch mode ", runFetch(runNumber), ", ", kindName$, ": ", runFrames(runNumber), " frames, average ", averageLines, ", worst ", runWorst(runNumber), ", late ", runLate(runNumber), ", fell back ", runFellBack(runNumber)
    EndIf
  Next
  NPrint "most balls on screen: ", ballsWorst, "; channels a sprite run may use: fetch mode 3 one, 2 and 1 five, 0 seven (the fifth run)"
  NPrint "the channels' data, two sets of 8: Chip RAM ", chipBefore - chipAfter, " bytes"
  NPrint ""
  NPrint "Compare fetch mode 3 bobs (the game today) with fetch mode 1 and 0 sprites."
  CloseFile 0
EndIf
End
